    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.56 score makes him our clear offensive anchor. Facing Nick Martinez and his 4.63 xERA, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a significant dynamic platoon advantage, which, combined with his premium #3 lineup spot, allows him to far outpace the rest of the unit. **Kyle Tucker** also presents a strong floor at 61.22; while his #8 spot in the order suppresses his ceiling slightly, his raw talent and a neutral-to-positive matchup against Mahle ensure he remains a must-start as we chase counting stats.\n\nThe remainder of our lineup faces a more difficult gauntlet, specifically against Espino (2.51 xERA), which has suppressed the scores of **Sam Antonacci** (45.78) and **Miguel Vargas** (42.51). While **Sam Antonacci** gains a necessary boost from his leadoff position and favorable wind conditions, the matchup against an elite arm like Espino makes these plays strictly marginal. **Jackson Merrill** (54.01) offers the most intrigue; despite a negative platoon shift against Gasser, his ability to exploit a slow-working pitcher (85% SB opportunity) provides the exact type of category-specific upside we prioritize for our 5x5 Roto goals.\n\nOur toughest roster management decision involved **Liam Hicks**, who landed just outside our active threshold with a 38.61 score. He was the primary casualty of the 40.0 efficiency floor; despite a helpful park adjustment, the combination of a tough matchup against Fried and a significant dynamic platoon disadvantage made him too risky to start in a game where we need to preserve our season-long caps. We continue to monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remain unavailable for today's slate, forcing us to lean heavily on the depth provided by **Andy Pages** and **Drake Baldwin** to bridge the gap.",
